# Credentials, read from ~/.config/pr-status/keys — a file kept out of version control,
# so that the config beside it can be committed. The format is the config's own, and any
# setting may be written here; a setting given in both files is taken from this one.
#
# This file can be a symlink, so the credentials themselves can live wherever you keep
# them. pr-status warns at startup about any credential left in the config file.

# From YouTrack: avatar → Profile → Account Security → New token…
#youtrack-token:XXXXXXX

# From Timely. The account id is the one in the URL after logging in; the access token
# comes from Timely's API settings. Both are only needed for `timely` reports and the
# `workdays` column.
#timely-account-id:XXXXXXX
#timely-access-token:XXXXXXX
